# The slider a `FieldKind.Range` is, painted: a bar across the middle of a
# track, and a round thumb on it at the value.
#
# Three pictures, one per axis. **Where the thumb sits** — every value from one
# end to the other, the same fraction of four different ranges, and every value
# a range cannot hold, which HTML sanitizes rather than refuses: outside the
# bounds is clamped into them, and text that is not a number at all is the
# middle. **How big the track is** — the twelve lines by one a browser gives an
# unsized slider, four widths, four heights, and the narrow tracks that say a
# thumb never leaves its own box. **What paints it** — one `Foreground` for both
# shapes, a `Background` behind rather than instead of the bar, and the border,
# radius and opacity of the box around them.
#
# The slider is drawn by the widget in all three renderers, which is the whole
# reason this case exists: the sheet's `:where(input[type=range])` gradient and
# `::-webkit-slider-thumb` on a page, `range:<min> <max> <value>` in the scene
# document, and a rectangle and a disc in the painter. A program can neither ask
# for a thumb that is not there nor build a range without saying what it runs
# between.
#
# Three things a reader should expect to see and not mistake for a fault. A
# slider narrower than its own thumb paints a disc as wide as the track and
# nothing travels, which is what a browser does with one. An `Opacity` of nought
# is a cell with a label and no control under it, because the bar and the thumb
# fade with everything else. And **a track shorter or narrower than one line is
# the one place the two renderers differ**: the painter shrinks the thumb to fit
# the box, where a browser's own is one line whatever the box is and overflows
# it. A thumb that fits is the better picture and a thumb that overflows is the
# better copy of a browser; below one line there is no size that is both, and
# the `6px` and `8px` cells are where that shows.
#
# The lifecycle is the sweeps': every golden compares, a renamed snapshot is
# reported as missing rather than as a difference, `--update` records it, the
# run after that compares against what it wrote, and an edit that moves one
# number fails the comparison.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs.

doc: "the bar and the thumb a range draws for itself, across every value, every size and everything that paints them, as 3 pictures with the whole record-and-fail lifecycle over them"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/slider", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "pass.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/slider/test/__snapshots__/range-values.diff.png"  exists: false }

# A snapshot nobody has recorded yet is reported as missing, with the command
# that records one, rather than as a difference against nothing.
edit {
  file: "lib/slider/test/pictures.buri"
  replace: "\"range-values\""
  with: "\"never-recorded\""
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/slider", "--force", "--filter=thumb sits"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "missing.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/slider/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: false }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/slider", "--update", "--force", "--filter=thumb sits"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "recorded.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/slider/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: true }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/slider", "--force", "--filter=thumb sits"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "again.txt"
}

# The negative twin: two more pixels of height on one cell of the sizes
# picture, which is the smallest edit that has to fail — the bar is a quarter of
# the height, so two pixels move it as well as the box.
edit {
  file: "lib/slider/scenes.buri"
  replace: ".Width(.Px(130)), .Height(.Px(24))"
  with: ".Width(.Px(130)), .Height(.Px(26))"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/slider", "--force", "--filter=big"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "changed.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/slider/test/__snapshots__/range-sizes.diff.png"  exists: true }
path { path: "lib/slider/test/__snapshots__/range-paint.diff.png"  exists: false }
